  "final_text": "All four steps are done. The dashboard has two panels, and the alert rule is enabled.\n\n- **Data view:** 'Kibana Sample Data Flights' has the time field `timestamp`.\n- **Dashboard:** 'S4-66adea38 Flights' (id `s4-66adea38-flights-002cd56f8e81`) has two panels:\n  - \"Flights over time\": a line chart counting flights on a date histogram of `timestamp`.\n  - \"Flights by carrier\" (renamed in step 4): a bar chart counting flights, split by `Carrier`.\n- **Alert rule:** 'S4-66adea38 Cancelled flights' (id `939903dc-aa96-4279-bbf3-29a24080b434`) is an `.es-query` rule on `stackAlerts`, checked every 1m. It counts documents where `Cancelled` is true in `kibana_sample_data_flights` over the last 5 minutes and fires when the count is greater than 10. It was created disabled, so I enabled it. Reading it back shows `enabled: true`, status `ok`.\n\nChoices I made:\n- The rule's query is a bool filter on `Cancelled: true`, with a page size of 100.\n- The carrier panel is a bar chart, not a pie.\n- I first titled the carrier panel \"Carrier flights count\" and renamed it in step 4.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
